  "description": "Change of use from a single dwellinghouse (Use Class C3) to a 5-bedroom House in Multiple Occupation (Use Class C4), including internal reconfiguration only with no external alterations.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The original dwelling has a gross internal floor space which fails to meet the standard of 120 square metres,  thereby resulting in the unacceptable loss of a much needed larger family homes within the Borough, contrary to Policy 8(i) of the Havering Local Plan 2021.",
    "The intensification of the site would generate high levels of activity and result in an unacceptable impact on neighbouring residential occupiers in terms of noise and general disturbance associated with the proposed HMO use contrary to Policies 7 and 8 of the Havering Local Plan 2021.",
    "A bedroom insufficient in size and there is no communal living or dining area which would be harmful to the amenity of the occupiers of the HMO contrary to Policies 7 and 8 of the Havering Local Plan.",
    "it is considered that the proposed development would result in an increased parking congestion in surrounding streets, contrary to Policies 8 and 24 of the Havering Local Plan and the guidance contained in the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy and time limits, amendments were not sought."
  ],
